WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:03.460
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.410
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.090
Wow, that really felt great.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:28.260
That's the last audition we've got for a while.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.180
Which means...

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.980
Spring break!

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.980
Not quite.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.030
Spring break doesn't exist for idols.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.690
Idols don't get breaks?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.110
It's exactly as I said.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.370
But in exchange, we get "off time".

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:46.990
Off time!

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.860
Don't scare me like that.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.840
It sounds so idol-y when you put it like that!

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.000
Okay, let's enjoy our off time!

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.350
Hi, signalize!

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.730
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.710
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.600
No, that's wrong

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.600
iie chigau yo

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.980
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.980
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.770
Do that signalize!

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:31.950
Something's starting to bubble up

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:31.950
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.910
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.910
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.450
So I'll believe in the present

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.450
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.620
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.620
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:45.960
Chance for me

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:51.260
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:51.260
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:55.470
It's just another challenge on the way

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:55.470
hora chousen matteru yo

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:00.390
Where are we headed?

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:00.390
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.140
Into a brilliant hope

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.140
mabushii kibou no naka e

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:11.400
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:11.400
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.780
Where we're headed

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.780
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:18.660
is into our hopes for the future

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:18.660
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:26.000
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:26.000
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:39.960
There are tons of famous shops along this street.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.000
They're all so fashionable.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.070
There it is! Fashion Central!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.970
I wanna go on a shopping spree!

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.110
Me too.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.210
Right?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.940
It's quite the grown-up spot, Ichigo-san.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.160
A place for refined ladies such as ourselves.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.450
Hey Ran, why don't you check this out too?

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.940
I don't consider that being "off". {Ichigo uses double quotes in a few lines}

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:03.750
Huh?

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.540
The city is filled with people, 
so we'd have to always be in disguise.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.510
Do you really consider being on guard like that a vacation?

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:13.890
I guess not! And what is your opinion, Aoi-san?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.710
It's exactly like Ran says!

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:20.270
Then let me ask you, Ran-san— 
what do you consider "off" for an idol?

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:21.900
There's no question about it.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:24.940
A hot spring trip.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:26.350
Hot springs?

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.070
Right.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.860
That's so adult.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.570
I can't help the feeling that's a bit weird for idols...

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:35.020
Distancing ourselves from work 
will let us rest our minds and bodies.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.580
This is what we'll do.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:42.270
Even Mizuki-san's secretly gone to
 this hot spring with the monkeys,

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.310
which gave it the reputation of being an "idol hot spring".

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.250
Is that true?

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:45.860
Yeah.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.600
Oh yeah, and I can even practice
 my hot spring reports while I'm at it!

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.010
It's like a two-for-one deal. {I've had enough of one stone two birds} {these are even in the bush}

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.260
Exactly right.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.470
How nice, and it'll help our skin too.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.390
And food will taste even better!

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.890
Now that we're all in agreement, 
let's go to the hot springs!

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.100
Yeah!

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.030
I'm getting started on our schedule right now.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.130
I leave it to you!

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.360
I'm off!

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.320
Be safe, and have a fun trip.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:12.490
Onee-chan, don't forget what I told you!

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.630
What's with that huge luggage? 
It's only a day trip, you know.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.440
But you never know what might happen out there.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.790
I've got my laptop and a charger.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:37.180
And just in case it rains I got us raincoats.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:40.980
A first aid kit for injuries, a sewing kit for emergencies, and...

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.370
Alright, I got it! Put that stuff away.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.150
Sorry I'm late.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.030
At least you're not running onto the train.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.360
Thank goodness. Raichi kept me up saying,

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.850
"Don't forget to take Aoi-neesan's picture!" until I left.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:58.650
Plus, I accidentally missed one of my transfers.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:02.560
I can understand that. It's awful when you run up the stairs just to see it get away from you.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.750
Right, right...

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.800
Aoi, your spring coord looks great.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.840
You think so?

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.850
Yours is cute too.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.600
Especially those red shoes!

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.490
But as expected, Ran's definitely got the best style.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:24.910
I'm not surprised.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.230
They're just my casual clothes.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.770
It's really hard to pull off overalls like you do.

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:37.790
Could you be Shibuki Ran-chan?

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:38.370
I am.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.610
Awesome, it's actually you!

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:41.750
Will you shake my hand?

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.850
I'll be cheering you on, okay? {er, not sure whether to keep this as a question form}

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.160
Thank you.

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:53.060
That's amazing, Ran. Even in disguise, 
your idol aura just oozes out.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.540
Come on, let's get on already.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.950
Ran, wait up!

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.970
I think we're fine here.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.200
It's so much more comfortable out of disguise.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.410
Nothing we can do about that, we're idols.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:10.730
Ah! Look, we're moving!

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.340
What are you, an elementary schooler?

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:16.100
But this is the first time the three of us have gone on an adventure like this!

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.750
I can't help it!

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.840
Same here, I'm getting really excited.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.600
I'll be sure to tell the Academy Mother for you.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:32.120
Yeah!

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.130
You're spot on.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.510
A perfect Johnny.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.790
Yeah!

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:37.580
And then Johnny-sensei said...

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:40.290
Ah! You're that girl!

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:43.100
Um, I think I saw you on TV...

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:46.020
Ah, your name's right on the tip of my tongue...

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.650
It's Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.650
Oh, was that it? Well, no matter.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.470
Can I get an autograph? Give me a second.

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:57.500
Huh? That's strange, I knew I put it here somewhere...

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.310
No problem, use this.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.050
Y-You want me to sign this?

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:06.010
Yes, and please address it to Fujiyama-san.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:07.040
Sure...

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:10.010
So you can write it mini-sized too...

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.670
It's all thanks to my training!

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:13.540
How do you read this?

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:14.820
It says "Ichigo".

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.550
Thanks a bunch. Keep up the good work.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.510
Yes!

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:24.520
Would anybody like coffee, tea, or perhaps a bento?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.490
Excuse me, could we get some over here?

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:28.440
Of course.

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:30.760
Do you have any seaweed bento?

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.010
I'm afraid we don't.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.480
No way you could get that on a train.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.150
Too bad...

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.150
Then which should I get...

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:40.420
I wonder if the deluxe yakiniku bento or the healthy variety one would be better?

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:41.990
Talk about polar opposites.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:45.910
Then I'll get the healthy bento, 
and we can split them between us.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:49.410
Thanks! And I think you should
 get the hamburg steak bento, Ran.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:53.660
That's just what <i>you</i> want to eat. I'll get sandwiches.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.580
Come on, the hamburg steak bento tastes so good.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.170
I'm getting sandwiches.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:06.420
I wonder why these lunches always taste so good while you're on a train?{just like yakisoba on the beach?} {didn't Minami-ke and OreShura both mock that;}

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:09.120
Perhaps because the scenery seems 
to become one with the flavor.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:10.940
That's pretty poetic.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:16.300
Get ready, Ichigo-san. Your gourmet report begins in three, two, one, go!

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:18.190
I-I'm not prepared yet!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:24.480
The first selling point of this yakiniku bento is, as you can see, the gracious amount of meat.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:27.200
This local Wagyu beef has clearly been carefully picked. {or Japanese beef}

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:31.350
Take a look! Now then, let's check the flavor.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:42.520
As soon as you take the first bite, the savory flavor explodes and fills up your mouth.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:46.270
I recommend this over rice, as the 
bittersweet sauce will combine well.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.670
And we're clear! Good job out there.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.130
That was too sudden, don't surprise me like that.

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:55.990
Your skills have leveled up from your training.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:56.980
That's right!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.610
Are you leaving this parsley?

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.240
That's my...

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:03.630
I thought you didn't like it...

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.240
It was my favorite part... {I swear we went over this save for last thing before} {we did, and I'm pretty sure Ichigo took Ran's last thing then too}

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.200
That's rare.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.530
My bad.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:10.870
Then I'll give you my favorite pickled veggies in return.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:13.190
Do you really think that'll go well with a sandwich?

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:14.750
If you try hard enough.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.130
Nobody can try <i>that</i> hard.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.130
Settle down, let's have some tea.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.630
Tea doesn't go well with sandwiches either.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:24.390
I guess so. Then let's be a bit more 
mature and have some cafe au lait. {what? more adult? really?} {coffee is sort of adult;}

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.640
Yeah, cafe au lait would definitely be better.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.900
Coming up.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:30.870
How about you?

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:31.620
Sure.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.270
Then all three of us will have the same thing.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.650
It's so sweet!

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:49.540
Look!

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.850
It's the sea! {I half want to leave this as "Umi da!"} {I only about 10% do}

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.370
I really wish we could go to the beach too. I want to let loose and go swimming.

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.340
Suntans are the enemy of idols.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.500
If you're going to go then wear long sleeves, use a parasol, and have anti-UV sunglasses.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.910
You'll need to put SPF 50 sunscreen 
on every part of your body... {you'd like that, wouldn't you} {what are you insinuating;}{you won't see this, but all the Nanoha finally got to me}

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:13.140
But I wouldn't be able to swim like that!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.410
You can't help it.

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:17.860
It used to be okay for idols to get
 a light tan for health reasons, {I don't know why, but "alright" bothers me}

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.450
but the times have changed.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.090
Then maybe I could make it popular now.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.280
Just maybe.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.010
We're here!

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:04.450
This <i>is</i> a train station, right?

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.000
There's really nothing out here.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.350
Where's the souvenir shop? I was planning on getting gifts for everyone back home.

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:13.340
It'll take us 20 minutes by bus to get to the hot springs.

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:14.450
Isn't that the bus over there?

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:16.340
Yeah, that must be it.

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:17.250
It's so cute!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.140
Let's go.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:19.970
Wait!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.550
It's been a while since I've gotten a bus ticket like this.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:28.760
And it only has one door, too.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:32.410
You can figure out how much to pay
 by looking at the board up there.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.390
This type of bus is actually the most common nationwide.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:44.110
I feel like the scenery and surroundings are so relaxing.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:52.120
It might be nice to live in an 
easy-going place like this someday.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:52.990
I think so too.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:57.870
This kind of scenery is really 
embedded into the hearts of us Japanese.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.810
What a beautiful field of rape blossoms! {One would normally ought to consider using "nanohana"}

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:06.930
Ah, so these are rape blossoms.

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:08.880
Mr. Driver, please stop the bus!

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:13.390
What's wrong, Ichigo?

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.010
What do you plan to do?

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:18.890
It's the first time I've ever seen this many rape blossoms! Let's get off here!

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.840
Being spontaneous sometimes has its good points.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:23.900
Yeah.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.180
Attention!

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.120
Denied.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.070
But I haven't said anything yet.

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.580
I'm just kidding. So what is it?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.290
It's a bit early, but lets have some 
tea while we enjoy the flowers.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.660
Sounds good. Let's have a flower viewing party out here.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:43.810
Ta-dah!

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:45.540
You're ready for everything!

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:51.660
One, two!

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:55.900
They look delicious!

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:58.060
I brought us some mini-tarts today.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:02.570
This one is cream cheese, and this is classic chocolate.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:05.060
This last one is fruit-of-the-season.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.940
I just can't decide, I want them all!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:10.070
I bet you wouldn't have any problem doing that either.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.070
Then let's use rock-paper-scissors to be fair.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:12.820
Bring it on.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.070
I accept your challenge!

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:16.920
Here we go. First comes rock—

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.370
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:21.130
It's a tie. One more time.

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:22.360
First comes rock—

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:23.960
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:28.590
Yay! I'll let you two fight it out for 
second. Now which should I pick...

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.710
It's finally time for our one-on-one.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.590
I won't lose this battle.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:33.960
First comes rock—

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.330
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:36.830
My win!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.600
So it was an "unhappy sign"... {excuse me, are you Johnny?}

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.600
Aoi, hurry up and pick!

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.500
But it's so hard to decide.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.110
I know I'm the one who bought them, but still...

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:51.560
The cream cheese used was carefully 
picked and sent from Bourgogne.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:55.570
The classic chocolate is a special 
import all the way from Paris.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.580
Delicious!

00:16:56.580 --> 00:17:00.410
The fruit-of-the-season was 
hand-grown on an organic farm.

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:03.710
Ah, I don't know, which should I have?

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.260
Then I'll pick for you.

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:08.840
This fruit-of-the-season fits your image, Aoi.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:09.890
So this one's for me.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:11.510
Hey, I wanted to have that too!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.010
Same here.{can you get any cuter?}

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:18.270
Hey, wait!

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:20.280
You're too greedy, Ichigo!

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:21.280
Give that back, Ichigo!

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:22.680
No way!

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.400
I guess this is the best outcome.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.770
Doesn't mine seem a bit small?

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:32.440
You started eating first, so it's only fair.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.900
Now, now, why don't you both enjoy some Earl Grey?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.780
What's Earl Grey?

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:38.060
It's a type of black tea.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.540
It's another piece of common knowledge for fledgling idols.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:44.540
It smells wonderful.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.780
This fruit tart is delicious.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:50.290
It's kind of lovely to be drinking tea
 while sitting among these blossoms.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.170
It sure is!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:55.870
Ah, I'm full.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:59.950
My grandma always used to tell me that I'd turn into a cow if I slept right after eating.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:03.680
It's good if you lie on your side 
after eating. It'll help you relax too.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.180
I wonder if my grandma's been lying to me.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:08.350
It's just to prevent bad manners.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:13.060
But if you go to sleep right after eating, your stomach will keep digesting and eventually make you gain weight. {what?} {she's an idol hakase, just trust her}

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:14.570
It's the enemy of Aikatsu.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.160
Man, she's fast asleep.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.760
She has a really peaceful sleeping face.

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:20.850
That she does.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:26.280
This serenity sure is out of the ordinary. {fuck} {hahahahahahahahahahaha I'm actually laughing so hard right now}

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:28.690
It's so warm.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:32.960
The stars are still shining even in 
the middle of the day, aren't they.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:36.720
Yeah. It's just that the sun's so bright you can't see them.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:41.480
Don't you think it's like a top idol shining so brightly that the rest of the stars are obscured?

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:45.100
An existence you can't reach even 
if you stretch your hands out.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:49.110
Then I think being a cloud would be fine.

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:49.730
Huh?

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:55.070
You may not be as high up as the stars, but you can appeal to the fact that you're always here.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:56.900
A special appeal cloud.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.410
That's how it is.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:04.740
That was a great nap.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.750
Ah! Aoi, Ran, wake up!

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.500
I got reeled in by the atmosphere and fell asleep.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.210
It's so late already.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:21.590
Oh man, we'll only have enough time to get our feet wet at the hot springs.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.760
I wonder where the bus stop is?

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.470
What's up with this schedule?

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:32.230
Two in the morning, one at noon, and one in the evening.

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:35.030
It was just by chance that we managed to catch it earlier.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:40.210
Forget about the hot spring, we need to get back to the station or we won't be able to go home.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:44.390
Sorry, I didn't have enough time to look up the local bus schedules at home.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:47.580
It's my fault for saying we should get off halfway there.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.920
Don't worry about it.

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:52.500
There's no choice, let's walk to the station.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.720
Looks like that's the only option we have.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.380
Sorry, I really am.

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:03.860
Then let's get a move on.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.430
Wait!

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.080
We should be almost there, right?

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.970
Looks like it'll be another hour or so.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.370
Oh well.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:22.150
Aoi, isn't that suitcase heavy? I'll take it for you.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.160
Huh? Don't worry.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:28.540
No, you packed up tea and all sorts 
of other things for us in there, right?

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:42.550
Sorry.

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.300
Don't give it a second thought.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:55.060
Are you three Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan, 
Shibuki Ran-chan, and Kiriya Aoi-chan?

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:55.810
That's us.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:21:00.340
I told you it was them! I've seen 
you on TV and in magazines.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.620
I choose my clothes based on yours!

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:06.320
Whenever I see you smiling, I feel
 like my spirits get lifted too!

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.330
Really? Thanks!

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:11.200
What are you doing out here?

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.390
We're trying to reach the station.

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:15.710
Mom, let's give them a ride.

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:18.990
Come on, hop in.

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:20.750
No, we couldn't...

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.720
Don't worry about it, it's still a while to the station. Hurry on in.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.280
Let's accept her offer.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.100
No objection here.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.130
Thank you for your help.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:41.360
That was unexpectedly tiring.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:45.490
But you know, even though we never reached the hot springs, it was a lot of fun.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:48.500
Yeah. We had a tea party while 
watching the rape blossoms.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:49.660
I enjoyed it.

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:53.120
Look, the ocean!

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:55.870
It's beautiful.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.880
Each and every one of the waves is glimmering.

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.790
It's like a field of gems.

00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:04.880
Let's all try to shine as brightly as those waves.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:13.010
It's from Dad! {WHAT}

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:16.270
He says he's coming home!

00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:57.870
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism.

00:23:58.730 --> 00:24:00.330
Our trip was so much fun.

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:02.220
It was full of unexpected happenings.

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:05.230
That's the fun part, how each trip is different.

00:24:05.230 --> 00:24:06.920
Next time let's make it to the hot springs.

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:07.460
Yeah!

00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:09.970
Journeys are about your companions.

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:13.340
What kind of person is Ichigo-tan's father?

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:14.810
He's cool and handsome.

00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:16.190
He loves good food!

00:24:16.190 --> 00:24:17.810
Nothing less from Ichigo's dad.

00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:19.680
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:21.380
The April Fool's Promise.

00:24:21.380 --> 00:24:23.800
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
